 "result": "All 874 tests pass on Python 3.13.\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed `test_package_zip_list` for Python 3.13, where `zipimport.zipimporter` replaced the `_files` attribute with a `_get_files()` method:\n\n- **`src/jinja2/loaders.py`**: Added a version-gated `_get_zipimporter_files()` helper \u2014 calls `z._get_files()` on Python 3.13+, falls back to `z._files` on older versions, both raising `TypeError` if neither is available (e.g. PyPy). `PackageLoader.list_templates()` now uses this helper instead of directly poking `_files`.\n- **`tests/test_loader.py`**: Removed the `sys.version_info > (3, 13)` clause from the `xfail` marker so the test now genuinely passes on 3.13+, keeping it xfail only for PyPy.\n\nVerified against both the sandbox's Python 3.11 and an available Python 3.13.2 install \u2014 full suite (874 tests) passes on 3.13.",
